Z||000000||Fat||02-15-2001||11:55 PM||||Hey dare, I've done some shopping and I've found almost everything I need to rebush the whole suspension.  From suspension.com I can get the ft. control arm kit for $54 and the r. trailing arm kit for $68.  What I'm not clear on are the endlinks and swaybar bushings.  They offer the endlinks in 84-87, but will these fit the 88?  Are the endlink the same front to back?  The Fiero Store sells two diffent sets of endlinks for the 88.  One pair for the front and one for the back.  Could someone clarify this for me?  Also I need to find sway bar bushings.  Neither Suspension.com nor the Fiero Store offers these for the 88.  Suspension.com says their sway bar bushings fit a 23mm bar plus they offer a larger set for $2 more that are greasable.  I'd like to have new sway bar bushings on the front and back.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Coop88||02-16-2001||01:24 AM||||I ordered polly bushings from suspension.com. Haven't gotten them yet, but they said to use the small bracket bored out a little bit for the front bar, since it is 1&1/8 of an inch. They also needed my rear endlink sleeve length. It was like 2&3/8 of an inch-not sure about that though. By the way, I drive an 88 formula. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fat||02-17-2001||12:54 AM||||There's gotta be some poly brackets available for the rear bar too, right?||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||02-17-2001||09:55 AM||||I ordered the end link kits from the Fiero Store and reused the sleeves from my old stock end links to keep the geometry the same. The end links from the Fiero Store had sleeves that were too long. I had to use a die to thread the bolt a little more so that the nut would thread all the way down with my old stock sleeve in place of the new one.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||c m west||02-17-2001||06:17 PM|||| we offer Delrin Bushings for the front and rear suspension for your Fieros. These bushings are far superior than polyurathane. Delrin Bushings are greasable and have a significant decrease in suspension deflection that would be found in a vehicle with polyurathane<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> ||||reg||1
